sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.25) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A Bluetooth adapter that cannot carry a headset's microphone or calls is
    told to the person, once, through the engine (sparky-stereo-problems):
    sparky-stereo-hardware-bt-voice.service runs at boot and when an adapter
    appears or goes (a udev rule), reads each adapter's state through the HCI
    socket (no root, no debugfs) and keeps a machine problem for an adapter
    that is up, BR/EDR capable and reports no SCO buffers (the CSR clone
    0a12:0001 with HCI revision 0x0810: the kernel's fake-CSR rule leaves it
    SCO MTU 48:0 and every voice connection is refused). The notice is in the
    nine languages and is cleared when the adapter is unplugged. ORDER 133.
  * A newly connected headset takes the sound and hands it back when it
    leaves: a WirePlumber hook (scripts/sparky-stereo-headset.lua, loaded by
    wireplumber.conf.d/50-sparky-stereo-headset.conf) selects a Bluetooth audio
    sink, or a USB sound card whose form factor is headset, headphone or
    hands-free, above the person's chosen sink without writing the person's
    choice; the setting sparky.headset-takes-the-sound turns it off. The script
    is wanted, not required, by a small virtual component: if it ever fails to
    load WirePlumber logs it and the sound is unaffected. ORDER 129.

