sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.21) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVIDIA's i386 libraries install by themselves after the apt run that
    needs them: inside an apt run, dpkg's post-invoke hook starts
    sparky-stereo-hardware-nvidia-i386.service (systemctl --no-block),
    which waits until that run has ended (DPkg::Lock::Timeout=-1), then
    installs nvidia-driver-libs:i386 and libcuda1:i386 at the driver's
    version under the edition's engine and tells the session; the run's
    terminal is told. ORDER 363b.
  * After a dpkg run of its own (dpkg --add-architecture i386) nothing is
    started; the problem is kept and says the next apt run brings them.
  * A failure keeps the problem with apt's output and the Repair; where no
    unit can be started, the problem says why.

