sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVIDIA's 580 path installs NVIDIA's 580 user space from the edition's
    repository, where the edition carries NVIDIA's own Debian 12 packages at
    its module's version: nvidia-driver and libnvcuvid1 are named at the
    module's version (580.196.07-1+sparky2+lc1). ORDER 354 milestone 2.
  * Where dpkg has i386, both NVIDIA paths install NVIDIA's i386 libraries
    at the driver's version too (nvidia-driver-libs:i386, libcuda1:i386),
    for Steam's, Wine's and 32-bit games' OpenGL, Vulkan and CUDA, and the
    dry run says so. On the 615 path they come from NVIDIA's CUDA
    repository, which apt already reads for every architecture dpkg has:
    a flat repository has one index, and its source's Architectures
    option does not limit it (measured with apt 3.3.3).
  * The 580 path installs sparky-stereo-cuda-repo with its lock, as the
    615 path does: NVIDIA's 580 nvidia-driver-libs depends on
    libnvidia-egl-xcb1 and libnvidia-egl-xlib1 at NVIDIA's epoch
    (>= 1:1.0.1), which only NVIDIA's repository has (Debian: 1.0.3-1).
    0.1.18 installed no CUDA repository there, so the path worked only
    where the image had already installed it.
  * Supersedes both packages numbered 0.1.18, which can never sit in one
    repository: ORDER 358's (in the round's cohort until this one is
    accepted) and ORDER 354's (not published). The changes of both are in
    this version.

