sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.18) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ORDER 358: report unreadable startkderc or failed systemdBoot reads in
    the shared problems engine. Do not apply the session zink override
    without a successful read; keep the desktop shell running and explain
    how to repair and start a new session.
  * ORDER 354, the lines below.
  * Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards get NVIDIA's 580 driver, the last for
    them, with the edition's build of its kernel modules
    (nvidia-legacy-580xx-kernel-dkms) and its own driver lock, picked by
    PCI ID from the legacy_580.xx table of NVIDIA's 615.71.09 README.
    Before, they got no driver offer. ORDER 354.
  * The plan window shows both drivers for such a card, in the nine
    languages: NVIDIA's 580 driver (the default) and nouveau (the
    edition's HDMI 3D at the card's boot clocks).
  * The 580 path installs its lock first, then the driver with downgrades
    allowed; no CUDA repository and no runtime power management on these
    cards. Every failure says what failed, why and what to do.
  * The open modules after the 580 driver: its lock and module are purged
    first.
  * Kepler and older cards name the NVIDIA legacy branch that last ran
    them; the edition does not build it, and the card keeps nouveau.

