sparky-stereo-hardware (0.1.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVIDIA's CUDA repository comes from the edition's package
    sparky-stereo-cuda-repo (its source, NVIDIA's key and the edition's
    pins), installed with sparky-stereo-nvidia-driver-lock in a transaction
    of their own before the driver, so the lock and the pins are in force
    when apt chooses NVIDIA's user space. Before, the setup downloaded
    NVIDIA's cuda-keyring, wrote the source and a pin of every NVIDIA
    package at 1002 itself, and the lock came only as the module's
    dependency, in the driver's own transaction. ORDER 338, ORDER 329's
    findings.
  * Keep a CUDA repository the person set up already, such as NVIDIA's own
    cuda-keyring, and add only the lock: two sources for NVIDIA's URI with
    different key files stop apt.
  * Purge what the run installed when the repository package cannot be
    installed or the preflight fails.
  * Read the NVIDIA driver version from a module built through Lean Code
    too: the published nvidia-kernel-open-dkms-stereo3d is
    615.71.09-2+stereo3d7+lc1, which the old pattern (+stereo3dN at the
    end) did not match, so the setup fell back to nouveau ("edition
    NVIDIA module has no NVIDIA version").
  * share/cuda-key.sh moved to sparky-stereo-cuda-repo's recipe.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0300

